<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_33" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_33">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_33" name="BPMN-33 | Product and Variant Maintenance" processRef="Process_33" />
    <bpmn:participant id="Cloudinary_33" name="Cloudinary — product image storage" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="UploadRequest_33" sourceRef="Upload_33" targetRef="Cloudinary_33" name="Validated image upload" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="UploadResponse_33" sourceRef="Cloudinary_33" targetRef="Upload_33" name="Stored media reference or failure" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_33" name="Product and Variant Maintenance" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-33, full catalog boundaries and shared-process rules; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.5 FR-CAT-01-05; supporting FR-PRICE-11-13, FR-BOM-07-08, NFR-SEC-03,08-09, NFR-REL-01-03,05-06, BR-24 and the documented Cloudinary image-storage integration. Implementation: index.html loads app/owner-products.js product/variant forms, confirmActivation and submit handler, app/pricing-state.js P.setPrice, app/staff-integration.js I.productAvailable, app/catalog.js and app/product.js. Current docs XMLs reviewed for convention/reuse, especially BPMN-23/26/31/32. SRS governs differences: preview image selection uses predefined assets; proposed upload validation/storage follows documented external-media support. No provider-specific transformation, file limit or upload endpoint is invented. Admin/Owner is the only editor. Authorized page access is an entry precondition handled upstream; no repeated administrator-access decision is modeled. Automatic permission checks remain at protected reads and saves. Local validation and exceptions are on the main diagram; external Cloudinary is a black-box pool with message flows, no generic broadcast signal. Scope is one catalog maintenance request covering create/update product or variant, activation/deactivation and subscription eligibility. Product name/description/image, applicable category association and per-variant label/active state are maintained without expanding independent category administration. Recipe/Bill of Materials and costing/final-price approval are separately owned by BPMN-35/36; supplied saved references/reviewed prices are used here, not automatically recalculated or approved. No BPMN-35/36 XML exists at authoring time, so references are visible rule/annotation references, not unresolved external call activities or fake embedded subprocesses. Product creation may save before a recipe is ready; no ready recipe means no ordering eligibility, not invented catalog-record rejection. Final prices must be valid owner-selected values where required for selected sellable variants; suggestions never replace them automatically. New subscription offerings/schedules belong to BPMN-34/03; this process records eligibility and does not enroll customers or alter paid subscription commitments. A combined product editor must validate dependent draft recipe/price/schedule changes under their owning rules and avoid partial saves. Availability reflects saved activation plus independent variant/recipe/stock constraints (BPMN-23 and checkout BPMN-09); activation alone does not promise stock or capacity. Failed writes retain existing catalog and transaction snapshots; media failure cannot publish a partially saved product. No deletion of historical products/variants, paid-order rewriting, price recomputation of purchased items, owner allocation, checkout, payment or marketing is introduced. Recoverable failures now remain in the same editing process with explicit review/edit/retry/stop paths. Recovery supports correction/resubmission as shown by the product editor and activation handler. The website reports changed data with instructions to reopen the form; no automatic latest-data refresh and draft reconciliation is claimed. Retry retains automatic permission/version checks, reuses successful media and known saved results under the SRS reliability safeguards. End events cover success, unavailable entry/loading, or administrator cancellation/stopping. No earlier BPMN is revised by this correction.</bpmn:documentation>
